<title>BELGIUM: Topcall  says sold 185,700 shares.</title>
<headline>Topcall  says sold 185,700 shares.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian telecommunications company Topcall International AG said in a statement it sold a total of 185,700 shares in an official offering ahead of its listing on Friday on European small cap market Easdaq.</p>
<p>The final tally of shares sold included a &quot;green shoe&quot; over-allotment option of 12,700 shares, reflecting the fact the offer was eight times oversubscribed, the company said.</p>
<p>By 1145 GMT on Friday 34,440 shares, or around a fifth of the total number sold, had changed hands on Easdaq, with Topcall's share price moving up to 3,110 Austrian schillings from an offer price of 2,850 schillings.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
